{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces/shell.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:51:01.324474Z","id":"c983ed5c665a5b757d8934fd14a95b231b2e0e3217a92501c92a5b3e08f15729","body":{"detail":"shell.d.ts's `triage` says \"ask each with `clax.threads.open`. Wait for those runs with `clax.runs.wait`\" and `@allow threads.open runs.wait` (lines 62-70). docs/contract.md:10737-10741 says a run of a host's kind has \"no operation of Clax's own surface\", so a host that registers this file gets a run whose prompt tells the model to call operations it does not have. crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts has no `threads.open` or `runs` namespace either (its `threads` has list/get/reply/resolve, :159-166). The file is the example `docs/BUILD.bazel` (`claxbot_surface_examples`) feeds to the clax-surface, clax-cli and clax-bot tests, and docs/usage.md points authors to `clax bot surface check shell.d.ts`, so it is the first file a host author copies.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":82},"content_hash":"c673fb17b46fb7d9495b559f1356bd4fd94762c7ec107cca3890b41636b37f7e"},"suggested_fix":"Either drop the Clax operations from `triage` (and its instructions) until binding Clax's surface to a host's run exists, or say in the file's header comment that `triage` depends on fan-out and Clax binding that neither the daemon nor clax.d.ts has, so a run of it today has only the `shell.*` operations.","summary":"The example `triage` kind allows and instructs Clax's own operations, which a run of a host's kind never has","tags":["review","review:claxbot-surfaces-deep","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces/shell.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:51:01.324495Z","id":"6283b607fd1626ef2af5a83cd4b3019d3e37247c4bf6a7e3637937a811125679","body":{"detail":"Line 4 says \"Nothing reads it yet.\" docs/BUILD.bazel's `claxbot_surface_examples` filegroup exposes the file to crates/clax-surface (src/tests/mod.rs), crates/clax-cli (tests/bot_surface.rs, `check` and `convert`) and crates/clax-bot (src/prompt/live.rs, which renders a prompt for it), and docs/usage.md uses it as the example of `clax bot surface check`. A reader editing it as a paper sketch breaks those tests.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"13363eb15b040ee5cf7e8d3cf3e71f163dcbdbc597c772a04ff72d9f354d8451"},"suggested_fix":"Replace \"Nothing reads it yet.\" with \"The tests of clax-surface, clax-cli and clax-bot read it (docs/BUILD.bazel, `claxbot_surface_examples`): keep it a definition `clax bot surface check` accepts.\"","summary":"shell.d.ts says \"Nothing reads it yet\", but three crates' tests read it","tags":["review","review:claxbot-surfaces-deep","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces/review.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:51:01.324523Z","id":"be9267ac98c61f57181d1172169fae10a0c9303807c4dcf7ce1a984cefc4360b","body":{"detail":"Lines 6-7 say \"Nothing reads it yet.\" docs/BUILD.bazel's `claxbot_surface_examples` filegroup globs every `*.d.ts` in this directory for the tests of crates/clax-surface, crates/clax-cli and crates/clax-bot, so an edit that makes the file stop reading fails them.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":8},"content_hash":"5e75003cb75ff3daf57cd57ae1e7817d148e8133d1da49963ca6b0c8f23c3178"},"suggested_fix":"Replace \"Nothing reads it yet.\" with a note that the tests named in docs/BUILD.bazel (`claxbot_surface_examples`) read it.","summary":"review.d.ts says \"Nothing reads it yet\", but three crates' tests read it","tags":["review","review:claxbot-surfaces-deep","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces/shell.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:55:56.852918Z","id":"c19639376af0a9e7a5418beb007d18e8a0ad013a9259d049fbbaa63ed5f3c7bc","body":{"detail":"shell.d.ts:66-70 tells the model to use `clax.threads.open` and `clax.runs.wait` and `@allow threads.open runs.wait`; its comment at :59-61 says only \"until `clax.d.ts` has them\". docs/contract.md:10740-10741: a run of a host's kind has \"no operation of Clax's own surface\", so the operations would not be given even once clax.d.ts had them. crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts:159-166 `threads` has no `open`, and the file has no `runs` namespace. docs/BUILD.bazel:19-25 feeds the file to clax-bot, clax-cli and clax-surface.","kind":"comment","references":"c983ed5c665a5b757d8934fd14a95b231b2e0e3217a92501c92a5b3e08f15729","summary":"confirmed: `triage` instructs and allows Clax's own operations a host's run never has","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces/shell.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:55:56.853427Z","id":"aaf1bc99fea3e9239f04c9d1e106fb5e94ecd56de006399368f46d0f47b0eb74","body":{"detail":"shell.d.ts:4 \"Nothing reads it yet.\" It is `include_str!`ed by crates/clax-surface/src/tests/mod.rs:31, crates/clax-cli/tests/bot_surface.rs:8 and crates/clax-bot/src/prompt/live.rs:14, through docs/BUILD.bazel:19-25 `claxbot_surface_examples`.","kind":"comment","references":"6283b607fd1626ef2af5a83cd4b3019d3e37247c4bf6a7e3637937a811125679","summary":"confirmed: \"Nothing reads it yet\" is false: three crates' tests include it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-10-claxbot-surfaces/review.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:55:56.853921Z","id":"e92e8df4e8b0721ecf9721d3c911f3a54d2b1ef0936e2a924798f9ac463a4297","body":{"detail":"review.d.ts:6-7 \"Nothing reads it yet.\" It is `include_str!`ed by crates/clax-surface/src/tests/mod.rs:33 (used at :61, tests/rules.rs:498, tests/canonical.rs:661) and crates/clax-cli/tests/bot_surface.rs:10 (used at :26, :92, :143, :592). crates/clax-bot does not read it (`grep -rn review.d.ts crates/clax-bot` finds only .qual lines), though docs/BUILD.bazel:19-25 exposes the glob to it.","kind":"comment","references":"be9267ac98c61f57181d1172169fae10a0c9303807c4dcf7ce1a984cefc4360b","summary":"confirmed: \"Nothing reads it yet\" is false; two crates' tests read it, not three","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
